course: dictionary
lesson: 12021
title: Chives, a mild onion herb
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A chive is a small herb. Its leaves are thin, green and hollow, like tiny straws. Cooks chop chives and sprinkle them on food. «Mum chopped some chives and sprinkled them on the potatoes.» The word chopped tells you the chives were cut into small bits, and sprinkled tells you they were scattered on top.
explain: Chives taste mild, like an onion but gentler. When you read «a bunch of chives», you can picture a small bundle of thin green leaves. When you read «sour cream and chives», you know a dip or topping is flavoured with them. Context clues like these help you picture a word even if you have never tasted it.
explain: The chive plant also has round purple flowers, and chives belong to the onion family. If you meet chives in a science lesson, the words onion family tell you the plant is related to onions, leeks and garlic. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: does «Dad stirred chives into the soup» still make sense? It does, so you are on the right track.
fact: A chive is a small herb with thin, hollow green leaves.
fact: Chives taste like a mild onion.
fact: Cooks chop chives and sprinkle them on food, such as potatoes, eggs or soup.
fact: The chive plant has round purple flowers.
fact: Chives are part of the onion family.
exercise: «Mum chopped some chives and sprinkled them on the potatoes.» What are chives? | A cake that is baked in a round tin | A kind of sweet fruit | A sort of hard round stone | *A small herb with thin, hollow green leaves
exercise: What colour are the round flowers of the chive plant? | Red | White | *Purple | Yellow
exercise: Which food would most likely be flavoured with chopped chives? | *A bowl of soup | A bar of soap | A block of wood | A pair of socks
test: Which family do chives belong to? | Rose family | Cat family | *Onion family | Pea family
test: «Sam snipped a bunch of chives onto his scrambled eggs.» What does a bunch of chives mean? | *A small bundle of thin green leaves | A row of tall trees | A group of people who like music | A box full of tools
exam: Ella says chives taste like chocolate. Is she right? | Yes, they are sweet like chocolate | No, they have no taste at all | *No, they taste like a mild onion | Yes, they taste like sugar
